{"title":"2025 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 22","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_(Similar_to_Solution_1_but_without_Simon&#39;s_Favorite_Factoring_Trick)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 (Similar to Solution 1 but without Simon's Favorite Factoring Trick)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5_(neat_trick)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5 (neat trick)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_6_(fastest)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 6 (fastest)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_1_by_Math-X_(First_fully_understand_the_problem!!!)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 1 by Math-X (First fully understand the problem!!!)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_1_by_SpreadTheMathLove\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 1 by SpreadTheMathLove</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(A_Clever_Explanation_You’ll_Get_Instantly)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (A Clever Explanation You’ll Get Instantly)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Thinking_Feet\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Thinking Feet</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Dr._David\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">12</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Dr. David</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-13\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_SquishBJ_(AIME_Qualifier)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">13</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by SquishBJ (AIME Qualifier)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-14\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_in_Chinese_by_SquishBJ_(AIME_Qualifier)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">14</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution in Chinese by SquishBJ (AIME Qualifier)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-15\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">15</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A classroom has a row of 35 coat hooks. Paulina likes coats to be equally spaced, so that there is the same number of empty hooks before the first coat, after the last coat, and between every coat and the next one. Suppose there is at least 1 coat and at least 1 empty hook. How many different numbers of coats can satisfy Paulina's pattern?\n</p>\n<figure class=\"mw-default-size mw-halign-center\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:2025AMC8Prob22.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/7/78/2025AMC8Prob22.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"412\" height=\"111\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/c/9cc654c2103ac569966e1cd010083ebc7421991f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 2\\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ 4\\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\ 5\\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\ 7\\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\ 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"351\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Suppose there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> coats on the rack. Notice that there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/9/a398005d35072ae993a9ac8b72dd8e746fcc416e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"41\" height=\"15\" /> \"gaps\" formed by these coats, each of which must have the same number of empty spaces (say, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />). Then the values <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> must satisfy <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/f/f2f58b4afd3bf4040ce37db8cb3b8e0f28530ac2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c+k(c+1)=35 \\implies kc+k+c=35$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"310\" height=\"20\" />. We now use <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Simon%27s_Favorite_Factoring_Trick\" title=\"Simon&#39;s Favorite Factoring Trick\">Simon's Favorite Factoring Trick</a> as follows: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/1/e118a88b36e69a43050d1d2e2e0b1aea81e8665b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[kc+k+c=35\\]\" width=\"121\" height=\"14\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/b/9fba8c51fb077682dfce0e17ae35facf3e425981.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\implies kc+k+c+1=36\\]\" width=\"191\" height=\"14\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/b/59b3651ae7165e96a48a493a6ef31386f3ddcb49.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\implies (k+1)(c+1)=36\\]\" width=\"189\" height=\"18\" /> Our only restrictions now are that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/2/db2398e8492c5b619950adb474609db3ef0ec3c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k&gt;0 \\implies k+1 &gt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"169\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/1/3b1940a9ee70fa8d844013460b6b21b34d1f78df.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c&gt;0 \\implies c+1&gt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"165\" height=\"15\" />. Other than that, each factor pair of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce5d3cbb9ab0a992ed503c2d4499e4f4af2f9d65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$36$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> produces a valid solution <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/6/8d6d37eb538c003ce52cc6801666df9da9e876b0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(k,c)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"42\" height=\"20\" />, which in turn uniquely determines an arrangement. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce5d3cbb9ab0a992ed503c2d4499e4f4af2f9d65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$36$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> factors, our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/f/72faa54256ff7fc6cda0608482a0530275f758de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9-2=\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}~7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"122\" height=\"30\" />. ~cxsmi\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Say Paulina placed <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> coats. That will divide the 35 hooks into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/3/0e3efd9b14723a92c2ae891fe27780d5f8e2b215.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" /> spaces and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/9/b699b78b2762427299268a6e62292091918430c6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$35-n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"53\" height=\"15\" /> empty hooks. Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/d/2ad6425693df46754377e65c475c11dc83ec62f8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[n+1|35-n\\]\" width=\"98\" height=\"18\" /> The values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> that satisfy this are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/0/af0ff5f62fb36cbbc2e7f53a1d1752ef6d3c806c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[n\\in{1,2,3,5,8,11,17}\\]\" width=\"163\" height=\"16\" />The answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/5/f158fbecb7d3114510997c9b35b5fc691deed602.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\text{(D) }7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"53\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let the number of empty hooks before the first coat be denoted as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p><p>This means that there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> empty hooks between all the coats. In every situation, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/5/ac5429dc4aa7ba1f3b20be4599a34c4220cc79db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" /> gaps, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> cannot be zero.\n</p><p>To solve the problem, subtract <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/3/f93f5c51ea4b04b4992b003b39479f29018f6bda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2n$\" width=\"19\" height=\"12\" /> from 35 (accounting for the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> empty hooks at the beginning and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> empty hooks at the end). Then subtract 1 (for the first occupied hook). After that, divide the remaining number of hooks by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/5/ac5429dc4aa7ba1f3b20be4599a34c4220cc79db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" /> (the number of hooks between coats). We do this because the first occupied hook is always after <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> hooks; we just need to check if the remaining hooks can be evenly divided by the number of gaps.\n</p><p>To clarify: \n</p>\n<ul><li>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/6/c766f9fce6070981e62f805a7cf7294baed4498e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />:</li></ul>\n<p>\\begin{align*}\n35 - 2n &amp;= 33 \\\\\n33 - 1 &amp;= 32 \\\\\n\\frac{32}{n + 1} &amp;= 16 \n\\end{align*}\n</p><p>Since 16 is an integer, this situation satisfies the conditions.\n</p>\n<ul><li>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/8/598a16d4b7dde3dec3a390109882d54bb0308ea5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 2$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />:</li></ul>\n<p>We can skip the the third step, as each time you add 1 to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, it decreases by 2 from the previous situation.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/6/72673c8e6dc9b8446157d4b4b3c9a4d8391ab995.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{30}{n + 1} = 16\\]\" width=\"86\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>This situation also satisfies the conditions.\n</p><p>Continue this process until the difference exceeds <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/8/968ea1fb96330a5738b62cef1b6eb879f73e573d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$35 - (2n + 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"108\" height=\"20\" />. We find that 7 situations satisfy the conditions. Therefore, the answer is 7.\n</p><p><i>Note: This method is slow but easy to check and understand.</i>\n</p><p><br />\n~LIBAIKO\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_4_.28Similar_to_Solution_1_but_without_Simon.27s_Favorite_Factoring_Trick.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_(Similar_to_Solution_1_but_without_Simon's_Favorite_Factoring_Trick)\">Solution 4 (Similar to Solution 1 but without Simon's Favorite Factoring Trick)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 (Similar to Solution 1 but without Simon&#39;s Favorite Factoring Trick)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Suppose there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> occupied hooks on the rack. Observe that there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/3/0e3efd9b14723a92c2ae891fe27780d5f8e2b215.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" /> intervals, each of which must have the same number of empty hooks. Let's suppose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> is the number of empty hooks plus the occupied hook to its right. Then, we have the equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/e/c8e35f5e7a275226e8f50f4f59ed9efd0dbeba0e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(n+1)m-1=35\\]\" width=\"144\" height=\"18\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/f/53f9c9fc0951ac7950e313b8a484e9c1400f7d30.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\implies (n+1)m=36\\]\" width=\"152\" height=\"18\" /> Our restrictions are n &gt; 0 and m &gt; 1. 36 has 9 factors, and two pairs do not meet the restriction. Our answer is then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/f/72faa54256ff7fc6cda0608482a0530275f758de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9-2=\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}~7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"122\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~Brainwhizz\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_5_.28neat_trick.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5_(neat_trick)\">Solution 5 (neat trick)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5 (neat trick)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Note that, for any possible valid arrangement of coats, there is always a set number of empty coat hangers between the coats. This is never 0, since then there would be no empty hangers on either side. So suppose there is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> hangers between every coat. Then, there is one coat every n+1 hangers. For any value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/3/0e3efd9b14723a92c2ae891fe27780d5f8e2b215.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" />, divide it into 35, the amount of hangers. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/9/7d9edb7e81fa59bfa771e44207b5c6036ab52c82.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[35/(n+1)\\]\" width=\"81\" height=\"18\" /> has a remainder of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, then that would be a valid arrangement for that value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/3/0e3efd9b14723a92c2ae891fe27780d5f8e2b215.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" />. This works for values of 2, 3, 4, 6, 9, 12, and 18. This means there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/9/6290a8014281892e00a094c752bd2b1df8aa73d2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}~7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"57\" height=\"30\" /> total possible arrangements.\n</p><p>-Arm123\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_6_.28fastest.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_6_(fastest)\">Solution 6 (fastest)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 6 (fastest)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Note that this simplifies to the amount of factors of 36, the total amount of places. This is 9, and take the factors 1 and 36 out to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/9/6290a8014281892e00a094c752bd2b1df8aa73d2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}~7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"57\" height=\"30\" /> total possible arrangements\n</p><p>~ Devansh M\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_1_by_Math-X_.28First_fully_understand_the_problem.21.21.21.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_1_by_Math-X_(First_fully_understand_the_problem!!!)\">Video Solution 1 by Math-X (First fully understand the problem!!!)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 1 by Math-X (First fully understand the problem!!!)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/VUL0T0YEAHk?si=eLNVR-1FBCXMlQ26&amp;t=7673\">https://youtu.be/VUL0T0YEAHk?si=eLNVR-1FBCXMlQ26&amp;t=7673</a>\n</p><p>~Math-X\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_1_by_SpreadTheMathLove\">Video Solution 1 by SpreadTheMathLove</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 1 by SpreadTheMathLove\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/jTTcscvcQmI?t=2200\">https://youtu.be/jTTcscvcQmI?t=2200</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_.28A_Clever_Explanation_You.E2.80.99ll_Get_Instantly.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_(A_Clever_Explanation_You’ll_Get_Instantly)\">Video Solution (A Clever Explanation You’ll Get Instantly)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution (A Clever Explanation You’ll Get Instantly)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/VP7g-s8akMY?si=q76L7lqj8IXEUGuL&amp;t=3152\">https://youtu.be/VP7g-s8akMY?si=q76L7lqj8IXEUGuL&amp;t=3152</a>\n~hsnacademy\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Thinking_Feet\">Video Solution by Thinking Feet</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Thinking Feet\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/PKMpTS6b988\">https://youtu.be/PKMpTS6b988</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Dr._David\">Video Solution by Dr. David</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=12\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Dr. David\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/ZIBTG4XzETI\">https://youtu.be/ZIBTG4XzETI</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_by_SquishBJ_.28AIME_Qualifier.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_SquishBJ_(AIME_Qualifier)\">Video Solution by SquishBJ (AIME Qualifier)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=13\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by SquishBJ (AIME Qualifier)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=EB-Uaexj9-4&amp;t=2207s\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=EB-Uaexj9-4&amp;t=2207s</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_in_Chinese_by_SquishBJ_.28AIME_Qualifier.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_in_Chinese_by_SquishBJ_(AIME_Qualifier)\">Video Solution in Chinese by SquishBJ (AIME Qualifier)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=14\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution in Chinese by SquishBJ (AIME Qualifier)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.bilibili.com/video/BV1fvuP6TEQE/?spm_id_from=333.1387.upload.video_card.click\">https://www.bilibili.com/video/BV1fvuP6TEQE/?spm_id_from=333.1387.upload.video_card.click</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=15\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_8\" title=\"2025 AMC 8\">2025 AMC 8</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_8_Problems\" title=\"2025 AMC 8 Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_8_Answer_Key\" title=\"2025 AMC 8 Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=42&amp;year=2025\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2025 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 21\">Problem 21</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2025